      "kind": "Decision network",
      "summary": "A Bayesian network learned over binned features and a binned outcome, completed by a decision node (short, flat, long) and a utility node; the decision maximises expected utility.",
      "implementationNote": "Bridge: score = expected utility of long minus short from the network's posterior over outcome bins, calibrated on validation; the price model is the posterior expected move. Differs from the spec: structure learned by pgmpy on the training span, utilities from training move bins net of cost. Expect: coarse probabilities from a few binned features.",
      "runnable": true,
      "unavailableReason": null,
      "implementation": "torch",
      "adapter": "decision_graph",
      "legacyFamily": null,
      "direction": {
        "mode": "classifier",
